{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0FPW", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:528ec04d422c5e67314ecd1091b7825ab680c000a6a66786d22e04ce5852976f", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe characterize invertible objects in the derived category of\na ringed site (both in the case of a locally ringed topos and\nin the general case).\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a4219984b539ae771260209462e17ce10dfe5be8bba36a35871195fc157e237d", "unit_id": "tag:0FPW:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0FPW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0002": "$R = \\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{O})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0005": "$R$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-category-summands-finite-free}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fe148e700ee49604f4a018f84927a477c7f017b0d8709150ffc3083b6609d589", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8072ef7ea2d9839ddd4199eb98a3a245260fc80b2266fd1260e45d0f101442a1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed site.\nSet <MATH_0002>. The category of\n<MATH_0003>-modules which are summands of finite free\n<MATH_0004>-modules is equivalent to the category of\nfinite projective <MATH_0005>-modules.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:214826c12035cbc1ff7ef8ce71d95d0ac24a19379b7a7cad821e569d20b2decb", "unit_id": "tag:0FPX:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0FPW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$R$", "MATH_0002": "$R$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{E} \\mapsto\n\\Gamma(\\mathcal{C}, \\mathcal{E})$", "MATH_0004": "$f : \\Sh(\\mathcal{C}) \\to \\Sh(\\text{pt})$", "MATH_0005": "$f_*$", "MATH_0006": "$f^{-1}$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Sh(\\text{pt})$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "MATH_0010": "$(f, f^\\sharp) : (\\Sh(\\mathcal{C}), \\mathcal{O}) \\to (\\Sh(\\text{pt}), R)$", "MATH_0011": "$R \\to f_*\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0012": "$f^*$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ec5f6abe0096abcecc8db993aa8e0118e15ac22401f56595abb0dbb2a88c15c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e7b341bd3d3c129d5dbc49fa3efaa3b53e2eeed551dedc8d0fcd582ef1f776ce", "source_text": "Observe that a finite projective <MATH_0001>-module is the same thing\nas a summand of a finite free <MATH_0002>-module.\nThe equivalence is given by the functor <MATH_0003>.\nThe inverse functor is given by the following construction.\nConsider the morphism of topoi <MATH_0004>\nwith <MATH_0005> given by taking global sections and\n<MATH_0006> by sending a set <MATH_0007>, i.e., an object of\n<MATH_0008>, to the constant sheaf with value <MATH_0009>.\nWe obtain a morphism\n<MATH_0010>\nof ringed topoi by using the identity map <MATH_0011>.\nThen the inverse functor is given by <MATH_0012>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6bcdae0978785beb1132e60e5727a365c3328f29c0008b09293a99e87422e475", "unit_id": "tag:0FPX:proof"}
